  "title": "India's Financial Resilience Amid Global Challenges",
  "summary": "India's credit quality remains strong despite ongoing economic headwinds, with balanced financial institutions and liquidity buffers expected to mitigate risks. The RBI's efforts to manage liquidity and address currency concerns further bolster its financial stability.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's credit ratio rose to 3.2 times in H1 FY27, showing strong balance sheets and liquidity buffers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) received Rs 1.91 trillion in liquidity mop-up bids, indicating demand for liquidity amid surplus reserves.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's economic growth in Q1 FY27 was 7.8%, driven by strong investment and real GDP growth of 8.2%, despite geopolitical and financial risks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
